# Infrastructure as Code — {{projectName}} on Azure

Deploys {{projectName}} to **Azure Kubernetes Service** with **Terraform**
(infrastructure) and **Helm** (the application). Everything is
environment-scoped and driven by `dude iac …`, which works identically on your
laptop and in CI/CD.

**If you just want it deployed, follow [Part 1](#part-1-first-deploy-start-to-finish)
top to bottom.** The rest of this file is reference.

```
iac/
├── terraform/
│   ├── versions.tf            # providers + azurerm backend (partial)
│   ├── providers.tf           # azurerm / kubernetes / helm
│   ├── variables.tf           # all inputs (sane defaults)
│   ├── main.tf                # resource group + VNet + AKS + ingress-nginx{{#if withPostgres}} + PostgreSQL{{/if}}
│   ├── outputs.tf             # cluster, registry URLs, app URL{{#if withPostgres}}, database{{/if}}
│   ├── bootstrap/             # one-time shared infra: state storage account + container registry
│   └── environments/
│       └── dev/
│           ├── backend.hcl        # remote-state location for this env
│           └── terraform.tfvars   # this env's sizing/knobs
├── runner/
│   └── Dockerfile             # the toolchain `dude iac` runs in — yours to edit
└── helm/
    └── app/                   # the application chart (backend, frontend,{{#if withRedis}} redis,{{/if}}{{#if withCelery}} celery,{{/if}} ingress…)
```

